198:
** ἀκρῑβ-όω**,
_future_ -ώσω, **make exact** or **accurate**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Hippolytus” 469}}; ἀ. τάδε **to be perfect in** bearing these hardships, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Institutio Cyri (Cyropaedia)” 2.3.13}}; **arrange precisely**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Ecclesiazusae” 274}}:—_passive_, **to be exact** or **perfect**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Ranae” 1483; ἠκριβῶσθαι πρὸς πᾶσαν ἀρετήν 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Politica” 1279b1.}}—Later in _middle_, {{Refs 1st c.AD+|1st c.AD: Josephus Historicus “Antiquitates Judaicae” 17.2.2, 12th c.AD: Eustathius Episcopus Thessalonicensis 1799.33, etc.}}
**2** **investigate accurately, understand thoroughly**, οἱ τάδ᾽ ἠκριβωκότες{{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Hecuba” 1192, compare 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Institutio Cyri (Cyropaedia)” 2.2.9}}; τοὔνομά μου σὺ ἀκριβοῖ; **are you sure of..?** {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Charmides” 156a}}; **inquire carefully of**, τὸν χρόνον{{NT|NT.Matt.2.7}}:—_passive_, {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|2nd c.AD: Vettius Valens Astrologus 265.3.}}
**3** **describe accurately**, τι {{Refs 1st c.BC+|1st c.BC: Philodemus Philosophus “περὶ παρρησίας” p.47 O.}}
**4** _absolutely_, **to be exact**, ἡ φύσις οὐκ ἀκριβοῖ{{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “de Generatione Animalium” 778a6; [ὁ ἄνθρωπος] κατὰ τὴν ἁφὴν διαφερόντως ἀκριβοῖ [prev. author] “de An.” 421a22; ἀ. περί τι “GA” 780b26.}}

